# node-npm: upstream's node:24.22.3-alpine (UPSTREAM_IMAGE, pinned by digest) with `apk upgrade`, npm moved to
# NPM_VERSION (the newest 11.x on 2026-11-26; the bundled brace-expansion must be at least BRACE_EXPANSION_MIN,
# checked at build and in the smoke) and corepack removed (it bundles undici 6.28.0; nothing here runs yarn or pnpm
# through it). node, yarn, the entrypoint and every setting are upstream's. The plain 24.22.3-alpine image fails the
# scan gate on 2026-11-25 on the npm, corepack and Alpine packages it ships.
# The scraper `fetch-rulesets` init container runs npm from this image.
# WATCH_ACTION=retire: when upstream publishes a newer 24.x release (UPSTREAM_TAG_PREFIX), the weekly upstream-watch
# asks for a scan of upstream's image of it; if it passes the gate (an npm with the fixed brace-expansion, no
# corepack), consumers pin upstream's image again and this recipe is deleted.
# Bump FC_REVISION to publish a new build of the same upstream tag; an existing tag is never overwritten.
APP_NAME=node-npm
IMAGE=ghcr.io/figurecollecting/node-npm
DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile.node-npm
SMOKE=node-npm
WATCH_ACTION=retire
DOCS_URL=https://nodejs.org/en/about/previous-releases
UPSTREAM_REPO=https://github.com/nodejs/node
UPSTREAM_TAG=v24.22.3
UPSTREAM_TAG_PREFIX=v24.
UPSTREAM_IMAGE=docker.io/library/node:24.22.3-alpine@sha256:116b800c3754b440ee0aa3ed2f20f5bf3d99a554bfd9adeea09ea8017f6e85f5
NPM_VERSION=11.21.3
BRACE_EXPANSION_MIN=5.0.11
FC_REVISION=fc1
